Z||000000||87ECO5||03-22-2000||03:21 PM||||<B>2M4 Dale</B> and I are working on another cookout - this time up North - to occur on 4/29 (a preliminary date at this point) at Mohican State Park outside of Loudonville, Ohio.  For the folks wondering where Mohican is ...<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Mohican.jpg"> <P>There's a rumor floating around that a new Ohio Fiero club will be using this cookout as their official debut!  Stay tuned for more details as they're made available.<P>So, who's interested?||||reg||1
Z||000001||fiero56||03-22-2000||04:28 PM||||You've probably realized this by now Scott, but I have a terrible time remembering dates and times, and I'm not on the computer with all the dates on it.<BR>Is this the same weekend as the swap meet down at Ed Parks' place?||||reg||1
Z||000002||2M4 Dale||03-22-2000||11:56 PM||||We could possibly meet at my place and cruise down to the park. (I think it's about a fifteen mile drive) You more southern boys could hook up with Scott and follow him here. We also need to set a time. Tabasco won't be able to make it till after 3:00 in the afternoon but he said he would meet us down there. ANY THOUGHTS ???||||reg||1
Z||000003||87ECO5||03-23-2000||06:39 AM||||A caravan up 71 sounds good.  Would love to see people's faces when four or five Fieros fly by them!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>3PM sounds good for eating but I'd like to get there a couple of hours before that.  My father and I will be fly fishing the stream that runs through Mohican during the last week of May.  I'd kinda like to map it out before he has a chance to.  Otherwise, he'll be killing me (and I have to pay him money for every fish he catches)!!!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Also, if I remember correctly (from being there about 20 years ago), there's a cave within hiking distance of the covered bridge.  I was never old enough (OK, I was never brave enough    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif">   ) at the time to scope it out.  I'd kinda like to do that too.<P>So, my suggestion is:  We meet at Dale's place at noon.  Hang out for a bit, gab about whatever (ya right - like it won't be Fieros!) then head to Mohican, arriving around 1:00-1:30.  I'll promptly pull the waders and fly rod from the Fiero and hit the water.  At 2:30, someone (maybe me if I'm not catching anything!) can start the coals.  We'll eat, drink, be merry, whatever ... then I'll have to cut out by 6 (I may have to work that night and it's a three hour drive home).<P>For the other "southern boys" that are planning to go, we can choose a place to hook up before hitting 71 (maybe the 71/73 interchange).<P>Comments?||||reg||1
Z||000004||2M4 Dale||03-23-2000||10:15 AM||||Sounds like a Plan !!!||||reg||14
