Z||000029||2M4 Dale||04-29-2000||11:37 PM||||Well my wife and I had a great time !!! 87ECO5 and I pulled off a pretty good little Fiero meet. We had a total of nine GREAT lookin' Fieros there. Including a 3800 supercharged 86 SE with a very tall wing, and a QUAD4 88 Econo Coupe. Also a 85 (I think) GT with a PISA fastback conversion. There was also a very cherry red 88 GT and a slick silver 87 GT. Ot Huster (FOCOA chairperson) was there with his POCI Servivor Gold 84 SE. COFE club members were just great !!! We have definatly let them know about our little FORUM here. Bunch of good guys and gals. Scotts 87 and my 87 fit right in and looked just as good as anything thing else there. Espesially Scotts motor WOW ! And Scott it was very nice seeing you again and meeting your lovely wife and daughters. We'll see ya soon Buddy...<P>87ECO5 WILLLLLLLL post some pics. RIGHT ? Some dummy in a black 87 EC forgot his #@$% cameras...OH WELL<P>Hey LennyB4 where were you ?||||reg||14
Z||000030||87ECO5||04-30-2000||09:32 PM||||Oh man, Dale!  What a hoot!  Great weather, beautiful surroundings (Fieros <I>AND</I> Mohican!) and lot's of nice people - ESPECIALLY you and your lovely wife, Christine!  Can't wait to hook up with you two again!<P>I wish we'd had more time.  I didn't get a chance to meet/talk with everyone.<P>I was able to get about 10 photos - one of each car and one of all nine in a row.  Once they're developed (man, I need to invest in a digital camera), I'll post them (most likely before Friday).<P>But, I'm gonna need some help placing names with the cars.||||reg||14
